{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:22082706 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:22082706 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"22082706","source":"MED","pmid":"22082706","doi":"10.1001/archinternmed.2011.555","title":"Cognitive behavior therapy, exercise, or both for treating chronic widespread pain.","authorString":"McBeth J, Prescott G, Scotland G, Lovell K, Keeley P, Hannaford P, McNamee P, Symmons DP, Woby S, Gkazinou C, Beasley M, Macfarlane GJ.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"McBeth J","lastName":"McBeth","firstName":"John","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7047-2183"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Arthritis Research UK Epidemiology Unit, University of Manchester, Manchester, England. john.mcbeth@manchester.ac.uk"}]}},{"fullName":"Prescott G","lastName":"Prescott","firstName":"Gordon","initials":"G","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9156-2361"}},{"fullName":"Scotland G","lastName":"Scotland","firstName":"Graham","initials":"G","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5539-8819"}},{"fullName":"Lovell K","lastName":"Lovell","firstName":"Karina","initials":"K","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8821-895X"}},{"fullName":"Keeley P","lastName":"Keeley","firstName":"Philip","initials":"P","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9028-2846"}},{"fullName":"Hannaford P","lastName":"Hannaford","firstName":"Phil","initials":"P"},{"fullName":"McNamee P","lastName":"McNamee","firstName":"Paul","initials":"P","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4540-8718"}},{"fullName":"Symmons DP","lastName":"Symmons","firstName":"Deborah P M","initials":"DP","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8625-1200"}},{"fullName":"Woby S","lastName":"Woby","firstName":"Steve","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0000-6295-8925"}},{"fullName":"Gkazinou C","lastName":"Gkazinou","firstName":"Chrysa","initials":"C"},{"fullName":"Beasley M","lastName":"Beasley","firstName":"Marcus","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6045-386X"}},{"fullName":"Macfarlane GJ","lastName":"Macfarlane","firstName":"Gary J","initials":"GJ","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2322-3314"}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5539-8819"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6045-386X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7047-2183"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8821-895X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9028-2846"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4540-8718"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8625-1200"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9156-2361"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2322-3314"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0000-6295-8925"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["outdated_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"172","journalIssueId":1895326,"dateOfPublication":"2012 Jan","monthOfPublication":1,"yearOfPublication":2012,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Arch Intern Med","title":"Archives of internal medicine","essn":"1538-3679","issn":"0003-9926","isoabbreviation":"Arch Intern Med","nlmid":"0372440"},"printPublicationDate":"2012-01-01"},"pubYear":"2012","pageInfo":"48-57","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>The clinical impact of telephone-delivered cognitive behavioral therapy (TCBT), exercise, or a combined intervention in primary care patients with chronic widespread pain (CWP) is unclear.<h4>Methods</h4>A total of 442 patients with CWP (meeting the American College of Rheumatology criteria) were randomized to receive 6 months of TCBT, graded exercise, combined intervention, or treatment as usual (TAU). The primary outcome, using a 7-point patient global assessment scale of change in health since trial enrollment (range: very much worse to very much better), was assessed at baseline and 6 months (intervention end) and 9 months after randomization. A positive outcome was defined as \"much better\" or \"very much better.\" Data were analyzed using logistic regression according to the intention-to-treat principle.<h4>Results</h4>The percentages reporting a positive outcome at 6 and 9 months, respectively, were TAU group, 8% and 8%; TCBT group, 30% and 33%; exercise group, 35% and 24%; and combined intervention group, 37% and 37% (P < .001). After adjustment for age, sex, center, and baseline predictors of outcome, active interventions improved outcome compared with TAU: TCBT (6 months: odds ratio [OR], 5.0 [95% CI, 2.0-12.5]; 9 months: OR, 5.4 [95% CI, 2.3-12.8]), exercise (6 months: OR, 6.1 [95% CI, 2.5-15.1]; 9 months: OR, 3.6 [95% CI, 1.5-8.5]), and combined intervention (6 months: OR, 7.1 [95% CI, 2.9-17.2]; 9 months: OR, 6.2 [95% CI, 2.7-14.4]). At 6 and 9 months, combined intervention was associated with improvements in the 36-Item Short Form Health Questionnaire physical component score and a reduction in passive coping strategies. Conclusions on cost-effectiveness were sensitive to missing data.<h4>Conclusion</h4>TCBT was associated with substantial, statistically significant, and sustained improvements in patient global assessment.<h4>Trial registration</h4>clinicaltrials.gov Identifier: ISRCTN67013851.","affiliation":"Arthritis Research UK Epidemiology Unit, University of Manchester, Manchester, England. john.mcbeth@manchester.ac.uk","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Multicenter Study","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Chief Scientist Office","acronym":"CSO_","grantId":"HERU1","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Chief Scientist Office","acronym":"CSO_","grantId":"HSRU2","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Versus Arthritis","acronym":"VAC_","grantId":"17292","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Chief Scientist Office","acronym":"CSO_","grantId":"HERU2","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Medical Research Council","acronym":"MRC_","grantId":"G0401181","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Fibromyalgia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Treatment Outcome"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Combined Modality Therapy"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Exercise"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Adult"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aged, 80 and over"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Middle Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cost-Benefit Analysis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Primary Health Care"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Female"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Male"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Chronic Pain","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TH","qualifierName":"therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Cognitive Behavioral Therapy"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/archinternmed.2011.555"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"source":"MED","reference":"Arch Intern Med. 2014 Apr;174(4):650","type":"Erratum in","orderIn":1},{"source":"MED","id":"22082710","reference":"Arch Intern Med. 2012 Jan 9;172(1):10-1. doi: 10.1001/archinternmed.2011.547.","type":"Comment in","orderIn":2},{"source":"MED","id":"22736666","reference":"Evid Based Med. 2013 Feb;18(1):23-4. doi: 10.1136/ebmed-2012-100781.","type":"Comment in","orderIn":3}]},"extCommentList":{"extComment":[{"extCommentSource":"CRD","info1":"22012003500","info2":"EED"}]},"isOpenAccess":"N","inEPMC":"N","inPMC":"N","ci